{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The 1/4-20 screws and M6 countersunk screws could complement my existing rivet nuts and metric hardware, provided their dimensions fit; the flush-head option gives me a useful reason to add another fastener.",
    "The short wood-screw assortment fits my pattern of keeping several practical sizes available for everyday repairs rather than buying a large quantity of one specialized size."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The long lag screws and pressure gauge serve specific jobs I am not currently doing; my repair history does not mean I need every kind of fastening or measuring equipment.",
    "Four 44-gallon trash cans are far beyond my current DIY needs, while another hundred M3 screws may duplicate hardware I already have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated fastener purchases seem to be treated as interest in almost any screw or washer, even though thread, length, head shape, and existing supplies determine whether I would buy it.",
    "My interest in tools seems to be stretched into specialized equipment, such as a pressure gauge or dial indicator, without a matching task in my recent work."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters: I would check whether screws fit my metric or UNC hardware, and the mixed metric and UNC wording in the M3 listing makes verification especially necessary.",
    "I already own several assortments and a caliper, so additions need to fill a practical gap; magnets and more precise measuring tools can interest me without being something I need today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my hands-on repair interests but sometimes mistake general usefulness for a compatible addition I currently need."
}"}
